WEBVTT

00:00.180 --> 00:01.785
Instructor: Another thing we can do is narrow

00:01.785 --> 00:06.330
down the diff to a specific file or files.

00:06.330 --> 00:09.660
So instead of just everything, right, all onstage changes

00:09.660 --> 00:12.570
or are all stage changes or all changes since head

00:12.570 --> 00:14.790
whatever we're actually looking at, we can narrow it

00:14.790 --> 00:17.670
down and say only in this one file.

00:17.670 --> 00:19.830
So currently, you know, we don't have a lot going

00:19.830 --> 00:22.020
on here that we would want to narrow down

00:22.020 --> 00:26.310
but if I do get daf, get daf, get diff staged

00:26.310 --> 00:29.550
as we saw in the last video, I'm getting two files.

00:29.550 --> 00:33.330
I'm looking at all changes that are currently staged

00:33.330 --> 00:37.710
but I could say, actually only show me the numbers file

00:37.710 --> 00:39.270
how that has changed.

00:39.270 --> 00:41.560
And that's exactly what we see.

00:41.560 --> 00:44.820
So as an example, let's say

00:44.820 --> 00:47.010
I have this really large project I've been working on

00:47.010 --> 00:50.160
I showed a couple videos ago where there's a lot

00:50.160 --> 00:54.360
of CSS and I made a lot of changes in this main.CSS

00:54.360 --> 00:56.010
and I wanna see what those changes are

00:56.010 --> 00:57.300
since the last commits.

00:57.300 --> 00:59.460
So I can do get diff head

00:59.460 --> 01:02.430
but there are other files I changed too, right?

01:02.430 --> 01:05.550
Index HTML, main CSS.

01:05.550 --> 01:09.240
But also there's another file I changed a JavaScript file

01:09.240 --> 01:10.800
here you can see that.

01:10.800 --> 01:12.480
And this is still not a whole lot of changes.

01:12.480 --> 01:14.070
Let's say it's been a couple of hours.

01:14.070 --> 01:15.660
I just wanna see the changes

01:15.660 --> 01:20.370
since my last commit to my CSS file main.CSS.

01:20.370 --> 01:24.270
So this is the path style/main.css.

01:24.270 --> 01:26.310
I can narrow it down, get diff

01:26.310 --> 01:30.780
and then style/main.css.

01:30.780 --> 01:34.140
And specifically what I want is get diff head

01:34.140 --> 01:36.150
because I wanna see all changes, staged

01:36.150 --> 01:40.380
or unstaged since the last commit in that one file.

01:40.380 --> 01:41.640
And that's what we see.

01:41.640 --> 01:43.800
So these changes are specifically

01:43.800 --> 01:47.070
from this file and we can see, right?

01:47.070 --> 01:50.170
Since the last commit I added these lines

01:51.030 --> 01:53.580
I added this line and I added this line.

01:53.580 --> 01:55.740
Really it's, I modified, right?

01:55.740 --> 01:58.500
I edited a line, but Git doesn't show it that way.

01:58.500 --> 02:01.380
It says this came from file A

02:01.380 --> 02:05.220
it's gone in file B and this came from file B.

02:05.220 --> 02:07.170
It's not in file A.

02:07.170 --> 02:08.003
All right?

02:08.003 --> 02:10.380
So that's how we can narrow it down to a particular file.

02:10.380 --> 02:13.290
I can also do multiple, for example

02:13.290 --> 02:15.690
there's also an index.HTML file.

02:15.690 --> 02:19.380
I just separate them by spaces and now I have two files.

02:19.380 --> 02:24.380
I'm looking at the diff for the main.CSS and for index.html.

02:24.900 --> 02:25.830
So this also works.

02:25.830 --> 02:28.080
If I wanted to see, you know, the stage changes

02:28.080 --> 02:32.010
I don't think I have any, nope, they're all unstaged.

02:32.010 --> 02:32.843
But if I wanted to

02:32.843 --> 02:35.520
I could do dash dash stage, or dash dash cache.

02:35.520 --> 02:37.868
And you know, other variations

02:37.868 --> 02:40.418
I can narrow it down to a particular file or files.
